OL,3,GNEWSAWe spent #23,000 on fertility
OL,4,Atreatment - now our embryos will be
OL,5,Adestroyed
OL,6,
OL,7,FNat and Nik Fraser-Edwards celebrated
OL,8,Ftheir son Jude's first birthday last
OL,9,Fmonth.
OL,11,FAfter rounds of failed fertility
OL,12,Ftreatment, Jude was a dream come true
OL,13,Ffor the couple who said they hoped to
OL,14,Fgive him a brother or sister next year.
OL,15,FBut now their dreams have come
OL,16,F"crashing down".
OL,18,FTheir sperm donor has withdrawn his
OL,19,Fconsent for further use, and the
OL,20,Fremaining five embryos in storage will
OL,21,Fbe destroyed after paying #23,000 on
OL,22,Ffertility treatment.
OL,23,APub: 09-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
